   Collected tables for weak reaction rates and neutrino energy losses
   creation date: Feb 18, 2010; DLR update: Sep 30, 2026.

   FFN: G.M. Fuller, W.A. Fowler, M.J. Newman, Ap. J. 293 (1985)
   OHMT: Oda, Hino, Muto, Takahara, and Sato. Atomic Data and Nuclear Data Tables, 1994.
   LMP: K. Langanke, G. Martínez-Pinedo / Nuclear Physics A 673 (2000) 481–508
   GMP: G. Martínez-Pinedo / Private communication
   DLR: Dasher, Lalit, Ravlic / FT-HBCS+FT-pnRQRPA (D3C*), this work

   This table: DLR replaces FFN/OHMT/LMP/GMP wherever DLR has both nuclei, except
   p-n (LMP), n14-c14 (GMP), ti40-sc40, zn57-cu57, al-6/al*6-mg26 (FFN); further
   DLR pairs are added for nuclei beyond them (Z = 6-41, appended at the end).
   DLR rates: lbeta+ and leps+ not computed (-99.999), so lnu is EC only and lnubar
   beta- only; EC without the 0+ multipole; computed for T9 >= 1 and lYeRho >= 5,
   lower T9 and lYeRho repeat the values at T9 = 1 and lYeRho = 5.

   T9     = temperature (T(k)/10^9)
   lYeRho = log10 of the electron fraction times the density (g*cm^-3)

   lbeta+ = log10 of the positron emission rate (s^-1)
   leps-  = log10 of electron capture rate (s^-1)
   lnu    = log10 of the total (positron emission and electron capture)
            neutrino energy loss rate (mev * s^-1)

   lbeta- = log10 of the electron emission rate (s^-1)
   leps+  = log10 of positron capture rate (s^-1)
   lnubar = log10 of the total (electron emission and positron capture)
            anti-neutrino energy loss rate (mev * s^-1)

================================================

